From: automation-platform-controller stewardship
Subject: [PATCH] controller: repair managed-role evaluations during sync

Implements: CTL-020 and CTL-024 (lab-content AAP-PLATFORM-DEFECTS F180)

Managed RoleDefinition synchronization updates the permission metadata, but a
no-op permissions.set() does not emit an m2m signal. Persisted RoleEvaluation
rows can therefore remain incomplete even though roles such as Inventory Admin
and JobTemplate Execute correctly include their view permissions. Team members
then authenticate successfully but receive empty resource lists.

After runtime managed-role synchronization, recompute each managed ObjectRole
and the user-assigned ancestor roles that inherit team permissions. Historical
migration app registries are deliberately excluded. This repairs direct and
team-derived evaluations across resource types without granting any additional
permissions or forcing a database-wide recomputation.

The regression removes the implied view evaluations for team-derived Inventory
Admin and JobTemplate Execute assignments, re-runs managed-role sync, and proves
both are restored.
---
diff --git a/awx/main/migrations/_dab_rbac.py b/awx/main/migrations/_dab_rbac.py
--- a/awx/main/migrations/_dab_rbac.py
+++ b/awx/main/migrations/_dab_rbac.py
@@ -295,6 +295,31 @@ def get_or_create_managed(name, description, ct, permissions, RoleDefinition):
     return role_definition


+def repair_managed_role_evaluations(apps, managed_role_definitions):
+    """Repair cached direct and team-derived permissions after runtime sync."""
+    if apps is not global_apps:
+        # Historical migration models cannot be passed to the runtime cache.
+        return
+
+    from ansible_base.rbac.caching import bulk_ancestor_roles, recompute_role_evaluations
+
+    ObjectRole = apps.get_model('dab_rbac', 'ObjectRole')
+    RoleTeamAssignment = apps.get_model('dab_rbac', 'RoleTeamAssignment')
+    managed_role_ids = [role_definition.pk for role_definition in managed_role_definitions]
+    managed_object_roles = set(ObjectRole.objects.filter(role_definition_id__in=managed_role_ids))
+
+    # Users inherit a team's permissions through the ObjectRole that grants
+    # membership to that team. Recompute those ancestor roles as well as the
+    # managed ObjectRoles that carry the direct permission evaluations.
+    team_ids = set(
+        RoleTeamAssignment.objects.filter(object_role__in=managed_object_roles).values_list('team_id', flat=True)
+    )
+    if team_ids:
+        managed_object_roles.update(bulk_ancestor_roles(team_ids))
+    if managed_object_roles:
+        recompute_role_evaluations(managed_object_roles)
+
+
 def setup_managed_role_definitions(apps, schema_editor):
     """
     Idempotent method to create or sync the managed role definitions
@@ -437,6 +462,8 @@ def setup_managed_role_definitions(apps, schema_editor):
     for role_definition in unexpected_role_definitions:
         logger.info(f'Deleting old managed role definition {role_definition.name}, pk={role_definition.pk}')
         role_definition.delete()
+
+    repair_managed_role_evaluations(apps, managed_role_definitions)


